<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Germany news: Deportations on the decline</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:25714d799e3e4d2df9112cad29369a4af1292ad7bf9ef9137dd326d5360f8f6e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T06:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126--231ad2fcde65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-deportations-on-the-decline/live-79860126?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite a decrease in overall deportations, more people were sent back to Turkey than in previous years. At the same time, Volkswagen is facing a fresh 'Dieselgate' trial. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong democracy activist Joshua Wong sentenced to 10 more years</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:08e2a08ecb27e2e9e44f3269bb8b67189fc3f5722053427b3697eb39539f0a9e</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T05:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898--15d97090ad43.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-democracy-activist-joshua-wong-sentenced-to-10-more-years/a-79859898?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Joshua Wong, once a teen activist and a poster boy of the "Umbrella Movement," is spending most of his adult life in prison.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>NASA's Swift space telescope plunges back to Earth in fiery demise</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57b69c01e9d53382b63aa80d7056ec492cd30d02ed52ea653ed9b38d7d770d2a</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805--86b86ba56b3e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nasa-s-swift-space-telescope-plunges-back-to-earth-in-fiery-demise/a-79859805?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">NASA's Swift orbital observatory fell back to Earth after running its mission for more than two decades. A rescue attempt to raise its sinking orbit had earlier failed.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Democrats take House and Senate from Republicans in US midterm rout</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7be0bdde02fc29f7286b308cce58fb1378becae6290fd46fa0328b9e2754cd16</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:15Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T23:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democrats-take-house-and-senate-from-republicans-in-us-midterm-rout/a-79859416--db0c6e2ab972.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democrats-take-house-and-senate-from-republicans-in-us-midterm-rout/a-79859416?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Democrats will control both chambers of Congress after flipping seats in Republican strongholds across the US in an election seen as a repudiation of President Donald Trump.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bavarian politician Hubert Aiwanger found dead in Berlin hotel</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b6bd3e22dd4beb246941d90d7392be38ceba762e259f8f6a6916436ebc63d03b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T21:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115--a5e0e6ba38b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bavarian-politician-hubert-aiwanger-found-dead-in-berlin-hotel/a-79859115?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Aiwanger was Bavaria's Economy Minister and the chairman of the right-wing populist Free Voters party. The circumstances surrounding his death are still unclear.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Winners, losers, the EU: Five takeaways from the US midterms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ed43f69443df0cb16be7aa071aa1ad71f0c0bcb677653486635cace6889e6302</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T20:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901--d5d91689d3d2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/winners-losers-the-eu-five-takeaways-from-the-us-midterms/a-79858901?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans suffered a crushing defeat in Tuesday's midterm elections, with the Democrats wresting control of Congress. What does this mean for US politics and the world?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>36 years later: Hungary opens Communist-era secret service files</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcd009b5a0dabfd236294a25cd39bc40293480d87561e2ce41e8bc0a85430ae8</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T19:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016--dc09772faa12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/36-years-later-hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-service-files/a-79858016?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Decades after the end of Soviet rule, Hungary is releasing all its secret service files. The disclosure is sparking fresh debate about informants, guilt and responsibility.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Examining viral narratives after the US midterm elections</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57843b8fc8faa668c796390a733245c049ef72795f566a1ffb02ae2609ab92db</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T18:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-examining-viral-narratives-after-the-us-midterm-elections/a-79851311--82139c11cec8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-examining-viral-narratives-after-the-us-midterm-elections/a-79851311?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Democrats celebrate major gains, false claims about election fraud have spread. Viral posts alleging illegal voting and election rigging are intended to fuel doubt about the integrity of the vote. DW checks the facts.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>French blood banks targeted by refrigerator cyberattack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9993f03ecca239c4a39b47fd541aae241bf64a61b166890cb9223bdae62f7920</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/french-blood-banks-targeted-by-refrigerator-cyberattack/a-79857981--e0b54ca9f23f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/french-blood-banks-targeted-by-refrigerator-cyberattack/a-79857981?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A cyberattack had attempted to destroy blood plasma by raising the temperatures in cold storage facilities past the boiling point.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The 2011 discovery of neo-Nazi killers aired biases in German policing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26422bfa84622f6e927b1a5787c132b0c74b9f893bd393dcde51d1e47a40f5f0</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T17:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781--949d4ea66003.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-2011-discovery-of-neo-nazi-killers-aired-biases-in-german-policing/a-79857781?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Many questions still surround the National Socialist Underground whose existence was revealed by neo-Nazi terrorist Beate Zschäpe on November 4, 2011. How has German society reacted to NSU crimes? Has justice been done?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Kosovo: Outrage as authorities accused of not helping femicide victim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:44a451e4ad3ee2c87ac6b9df837a73afb3a6d226c80050c568627399e43709e4</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T16:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726--34859fc77a44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kosovo-outrage-as-authorities-accused-of-not-helping-femicide-victim/a-79856726?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Despite reporting her husband to the police and pleading for protection, Arlinda Zekaj was brutally murdered. Now, thousands in Kosovo are protesting what they say is a dramatic failure of state institutions.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba8bff90f9ee9c4f849f9f1f6ddfc4fc0ea6e930442c964658ca218a637f3b63</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Africa's shifting role in the global drug trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f402d157499114f816dee9cb1d9902fdb9e025ce36e623e62de7e6081633226</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720--a33472b9e48a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/africa-s-shifting-role-in-the-global-drug-trade/a-79847720?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent discoveries of meth labs suggest parts of Africa are moving beyond drug transit and becoming sites of synthetic drug production.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Harry Potter films turns 25 ahead of new TV series' release</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d08cf29079fc5cd472ce6b89230e73f1450e0c4131caa9304c5fc99eb6b36a67</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130--db1dcb8d550c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/harry-potter-films-turns-25-ahead-of-new-tv-series-release/a-79856130?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In 2001, "Harry Potter and the Sorcerer's Stone" hit cinemas and took the world by storm. Today, anticipation for the new series is high, but its creator, J.K. Rowling, remains a controversial figure.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>What the Democrats' midterms win means for the US economy and Trump</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1ad511d9f5729eecd60729bb162daba672fd467ae25acec617ee982529b53c5b</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716--124f824b0e07.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-democrats-midterms-win-means-for-the-us-economy-and-trump/a-79853716?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From high oil prices and data centers to tariffs and mounting debt, economic concerns played a key role in the crushing defeat of President Donald Trump's Republicans. So can the Democrats now make a difference?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU says Montenegro on track to become bloc's next member state by 2028</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70965ce87333445845a846d9520f576acf0bb8091bfa994a8aa247b828886ef</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011--2c07b9ca6077.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-says-montenegro-on-track-to-become-bloc-s-next-member-state-by-2028/a-79855011?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Brussels says Montenegro is likely to become the EU's 28th member state, followed by Albania and Moldova. It said Ukraine needed to speed up reforms and offered fresh hope to Serbia following elections last month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Leading ice hockey nations, sponsors oppose Russia's return</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:672eeba8d5de5a10ef28cd4fb22320790f37eb07bb124699f1f51b673da81859</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T13:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742--b5324aaa0f6e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/leading-ice-hockey-nations-sponsors-oppose-russia-s-return/a-79853742?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey's governing body says the impact of a court decision forcing it to reinstate Russia presents "significant practical and sporting challenges." Several leading nations say they won't play against Russian teams.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Commerce chief hopes for more stable US trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f5e9d31121c78b6a3a7ac42231fcb36f283382bc17ab2e54366ca166337c5d2</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127--6b9f63120529.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-commerce-chief-hopes-for-more-stable-us-trade/live-79854127?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German business is pinning its hopes on greater stability in US trade relations after a midterm blow for Donald Trump. Meanwhile, Germany's automakers appear to be feeling less gloomy than in recent years.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia deploys troops to Jakarta after wiretapping allegations</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fbc14b466aa4fb2e636a507e1ad5edc01ce0b5b1a13d3195e9efaa0910f1fec8</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779--6f55d522a605.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-deploys-troops-to-jakarta-after-wiretapping-allegations/a-79853779?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indonesian troops are being stationed in Jakarta amid wiretapping allegations implicating the president's chief of staff. Suspects are being accused of illegally tapping the president's phones.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'largely true' Iran war led to Republican midterm loss</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3228e31850da41742b7410b9d98df69d1a378bc8b79f03649e997d68a97a272</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:03:24Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-largely-true-iran-war-led-to-republican-midterm-loss/live-79829440--7f589033d85e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-largely-true-iran-war-led-to-republican-midterm-loss/live-79829440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Democrats won both the House and Senate in a blowout for Republicans, President Donald Trump admitted fuel prices brought on by the Iran war impacted the outcome, but stuck by his decision.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary opens communist-era secret police files identifying informants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ac2972c1be843fdd3dbd466f8eb55036a8a63ac9ab73fd19797f9d13415e7ab</id><updated>2026-11-05T07:02:09Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T12:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-police-files-identifying-informants/a-79853492--bea146ac21f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-opens-communist-era-secret-police-files-identifying-informants/a-79853492?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The archives name thousands of former informants who spied on citizens for the state security services during decades of one-party rule. The prime minister said "many families will now face difficult information."</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
